        <p class="eyebrow">About this episode</p>
        <h2>A spontaneous phone call becomes an honest conversation about whole-person health.</h2>
        <p class="lede">When Mikel misses a call from his friend Matthew during a recording session, the group calls him back and invites him into an unplanned mental-health check-in.</p>
        <p>Joined by Zach and Josh, Matthew reflects on a challenging season, the role prayer plays when financial pressure and uncertainty create stress, and how remembering past moments of provision helps him release what he cannot control.</p>
        <p>The conversation turns to the people we trust. Matthew shares why he keeps a small, intentional circle of friends and how their response during difficult seasons reveals who can offer honest support without judgment. Together, the group explores what healthy vulnerability can look like in everyday friendships.</p>
        <p>They also connect mental health with physical activity, nutrition, spiritual health, and social support. From exercise and consistency to seeking clarity about purpose, the episode shows how each part of life can influence the others—and why a simple conversation with a friend can be a meaningful place to begin.</p>

        <h3>In this episode</h3>
        <ul class="topic-list">
          <li>Turning a spontaneous phone call into a genuine mental-health check-in</li>
          <li>Prayer, music, and reflection as responses to stress and anxiety</li>
          <li>Navigating financial uncertainty without carrying every outcome alone</li>
          <li>How stress can affect both emotional and physical well-being</li>
          <li>Building a small, intentional circle of trustworthy friends</li>
          <li>Learning who can respond with support during difficult seasons</li>
          <li>The relationship between physical activity and mental health</li>
          <li>Nutrition, consistency, and making changes alongside other people</li>
          <li>Pursuing purpose with patience, prayer, and clarity</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

